<title>USA: Burlington Q4 hurt by higher fuel costs.</title>
<headline>Burlington Q4 hurt by higher fuel costs.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Burlington Northern Santa Fe Corp Tuesday said its fourth quarter results were hurt by a $29 million increase in fuel expense, reflecting a 19 percent increase in the cost of fuel per gallon.</p>
<p>Burlington Northern Tuesday reported fourth quarter 1996 net income of $244 million, or $1.56 per share, compared with adjusted fourth quarter 1995 net income of $203 million or $1.32 per share.</p>
<p>For the year, the company said its fuel expense was $64 million higher than 1995 reflecting an 11 percent increase in cost per gallon.</p>
</text>
